Bhavantah - you people; Etat - this; Vijnay - knowing; Deha-adi - physical body and other things; Utpadyam - subject to birth;
Anta-vat - about the end; Mam - to me; Yajantah - while worshiping; Adhvaraih - through Vedic sacrifices; Yuktah - united; Vimala buddhi - with pure intellect;
United; Prajaah - of one's subjects; Dharmena - according to religious principles; Rakshyatha - should protect. Understanding that this is the beginning and end of the physical body and everything associated with it,
worship me through Vedic sacrifices and protect your subjects with pure intellect according to the principles of Dharma. Santhvanantaha janataanthanusukham duhkham bhavabhavau.
Receive, receive, and contemplate with your mind. 22. Meaning of the word:

Santanvantah - while producing; Praja - of progeny; Tantun - fibers (generations); Sukham - happiness; Dukham - sorrow; Bhavah - birth;
Abhavau - as death; Praptam - having attained; Jaan - as; Saha - as; Sevantah - while accepting; Mat-Chittaah - upon me;
Stabilizing one's mind; Vicharishyath - one should wander here and there. Generating generations of generations of offspring and facing happiness and sorrow, birth and death,
you people, while spending your lives, always keep your minds fixed on me. Those who are sad, who have attachment to the body, and who are of the nature of a self-controlled man. Mayaavesya manah samyangamante brahma yasyatha. 23 ज़a. Meaning of the word

Udasinaah - other-minded; cha-tatha; deha-adau - towards the body, etc.; atma-araamaah - self-content; dhruta - held firmly; vrataha - one's vows; mayi - in me; aveshya - concentrating; manah - the mind; samyak - completely; mam - to me;
Ante - in the end; Brahma - the ultimate truth; yasyatha - you will attain.
.

Become detached from the body and everything associated with it. Remaining contented, keep your mind
Concentrating on me, follow your vows with firmness. In this way, you people will ultimately attain me, the supreme truth.
